WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.740
If you want to hear about how Richie's teenage
years are documented in another Stephen King

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.260
novel, then stick around to the end of this
video.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:16.180
You went online, clicked on this video, basically
dragged me out here to this studio, and now

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:18.590
I'm gonna have to analyse this ******* character.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:22.250
So welcome to Horror History, my name is Zac
Morris, you may remember me from Saved by

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.849
the Deathbell, and in today's lesson I'll
be breaking down the story of Richie Tozier.

00:00:25.849 --> 00:00:29.740
Everybody else seemed to be more interested
in breaking down the glasses of Richie Tozier.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.860
He's constantly bullied for his spectacles
and his loud mouth, but despite his poor eyesight,

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:36.330
I think it's Richie's eyes that are the key
to understanding him.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:40.100
With that in mind, let's take it back to Richie's
days as a young rock and roller.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:45.280
Richard Tozier was born in the year 1945.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:49.190
As far as we know, Richie was the only son
of a dentist named Wentworth and his wife

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:50.190
Maggie.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:54.260
Maggie had hoped to have a girl and isn’t
always a fan of Richie’s boisterous personality.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:58.780
Richie always had poor eyesight and seems
to suffer from Ommetaphobia, or a fear related

00:00:58.780 --> 00:00:59.809
to one’s eyes.

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:03.510
One time when he was very young, he dreamt
that he poked his eye full of blood, and when

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.640
he woke up he was actually relieved that he’d
only wet the bed.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.790
Richie had a good relationship with his father.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:12.390
Wentworth never went easy on Richie, but he
understood his son and would sometimes even

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:13.530
do voices with him.

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:17.030
Wentworth took Richie out to see the Paul
Bunyan statue when it was first unveiled in

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:18.340
Derry’s City Center.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.010
As a kid, Richie would most often hang out
with his friend Stan Uris, and the two would

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:25.310
sometimes to go the Barrens to do stuff with
Bill Denbrough and Eddie Kaspbrak.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.590
There aren’t really any Richie and Stan
scenes in the book, but we’re given the

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:32.890
impression that they’re close in both movies
-- they show up as a pair in the 1990 version

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:37.290
and Richie is the only one to attend Stan’s
Bar Mitzvah in the 2017 adaptation.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:39.880
Richie was best known for his voice impressions,
which included:

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:44.190
-Kinky Briefcase, Sexual Accountant
-Jim, from Huckleberry Finn

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:46.870
-The German Commandant
-Toodles, the English Senator / Butler

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:49.750
"Now, pip-pip and talio my good fellows!"

00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:51.420
-The Movie Newsreel Narrator

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.800
"Newsflash Ben, school's out for summa!"

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.740
-Granny Grunt
-Poncho Vanilla Voice

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.730
"Doesn't smell like caca to me señor."

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:58.810
-Pickenanny
-Chinese Cooley

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:03.060
-And many, many more celebrity voice impressions
that probably would have had the SJWs up in

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.420
a ****ing rage had the internet been around
back then, but it wasn’t so instead Richie’s

00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:10.090
impressions, which most agreed were rather
pedestrian...

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:11.760
"Your voices all sound the same Richie."

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.510
...seemed to piss off the bullies of Derry
more than anyone.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:18.150
They were constantly chasing him, beating
him up, breaking his glasses and disliking

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:19.800
his videos without even watching them!

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:21.800
OK, I made that last one up.

00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:25.900
But one day at school the leader of the bullies,
Henry Bowers, slipped on a puddle and yeah,

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:27.100
let me just play the clip.

00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:38.300
"Hey, way to go Banana Heels!"

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:41.080
How was this kid considered a Loser?

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:44.110
If he grew up when I did he would have been
considered a ****ing legend.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:47.330
So after school that day the bullies were
looking for him, and they chased him all the

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:51.040
way through town to Freese’s department
store, where he hid in the toy department

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.730
and then snuck out the emergency exit.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:56.550
The scene is not in any movie so far, but
Richie’s Friese’s t-shirt in the 2017

00:02:56.550 --> 00:03:00.410
film, suggests that maybe he hid there in
the book because he knew the ins and out of

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.410
the place.

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.870
Now Stan might be Jewish, but Richie is probably
the most relatable character for me because

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:09.750
of his love for horror movies, rock and roll
and his overwhelmingly charming personalit--

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:10.880
OK fine take that one out.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:12.120
"It is a gift!"

00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:18.680
But Richie sees a poster for a rock show he
wants to go to, but knows that his mom wouldn’t

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:23.099
let him, so he sits on a bench in the sun
and the Paul Bunyan statue moves and stares

00:03:23.099 --> 00:03:25.569
him straight in the face, threatening to eat
him!

00:03:25.569 --> 00:03:29.750
The ground would shake with Paul’s enormous
steps, and Paul destroyed the bench Richie

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:32.790
had been sitting on moments before with his
giant axe.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.739
When he looked back, the scene was normal.

00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:38.040
This was obviously his first encounter with
IT, but Richie is somehow able to convince

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.550
himself that it was just a dream.

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:42.440
He probably does have bad dreams with all
the scary movies he’s watching from such

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:46.240
a young age and his obsession with media can
be both a strength and a point of weakness

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:47.240
for him.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:50.580
This is why I think Richie’s eyes and glasses
are so significant, because it’s generally

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:55.800
the things he sees in movies or on TV that
scare him, but it's also the things he sees

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:59.900
on those same programs that help him fight
back against It, whether it be with his voice

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.410
impressions or by using tactics that only
work in the movies.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:06.890
In this case though, nothing really comes
of it, but the experience sticks in the back

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:07.890
of his mind.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.530
On the first day of summer, Richie has to
stay back and help his dad clean out their

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:15.030
attic, but the next day, Richie and Stan show
up to help Bill, Eddie and Ben build a dam

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:16.590
in the stream in the Barrens.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:20.129
Richie enjoys hanging out with them there
because his antics get him in real world trouble,

00:04:20.129 --> 00:04:21.930
but not in the Barrens.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:26.249
That afternoon, each of them reveals their
personal encounters with Pennywise, but Richie,

00:04:26.249 --> 00:04:28.990
still under the belief that his was a dream,
has nothing to share.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:33.069
They are interrupted by Mr. Nell, the Irish
Derry police officer, who is angry at them

00:04:33.069 --> 00:04:35.400
for backing up the drainage system with their
dam.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.960
Richie demonstrates his inability to control
his ever-running mouth.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:41.860
[“How’s things back in the auld country,
Mr. Nell?” it bugled.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:47.139
“Ah, yer a sight for sore eyes, sure an
begorrah, yer a lovely man, a credit to the

00:04:47.139 --> 00:04:48.199
auld sod—”]

00:04:48.199 --> 00:04:50.879
Only Bill telling Richie to shut up makes
him stop.

00:04:50.879 --> 00:04:54.840
Mr. Nell ends up making them clear it up and
agrees not to rat them out if they do.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:57.879
That evening, Bill and Richie are walking
home together, and Richie asks to see the

00:04:57.879 --> 00:04:59.889
picture of Georgie that winked at Bill.

00:04:59.889 --> 00:05:03.580
After talking about it with Richie, Bill starts
to feel like he’s in a better place.

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:07.080
This is the first of many examples of Richie
offering support to Bill.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:11.020
After being the seer of the group -- this
is the next most important aspect of Richie’s

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:14.720
character in that he’s there for his friends,
especially Bill -- we continue to see more

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:15.740
of that throughout the story.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:20.240
It isn’t until they actually arrive in Georgie’s
room that Richie starts to freak himself out a little

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:21.220
bit himself.

00:05:21.229 --> 00:05:24.990
He can see the dried blood on the pages of
the album and feel the cold touch of the pages.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:28.430
Georgie’s school picture is missing, but
there is a photo from the olden days of Derry

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.659
with two sailors.

00:05:29.659 --> 00:05:30.819
They were Richie and Bill.

00:05:30.819 --> 00:05:34.150
The photo comes to life, like a movie, and
they see Pennywise pop up over the edge of

00:05:34.150 --> 00:05:38.310
the canal like a jack-in-the-box - only it
has Georgie’s face…

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:42.319
Richie saves Bill by pulling him out of the
photo after her tries to reach his hand inside,

00:05:42.319 --> 00:05:43.819
and they flee from Georgie’s room.

00:05:43.819 --> 00:05:48.430
This is the first time Richie realizes that
what they all saw were not just stories or

00:05:48.430 --> 00:05:52.160
movies… the thing that had been haunting
Derry was a monster.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:01.399
Richie Tozier would have been subscribed to
this channel with Deathbell notifications

00:06:01.399 --> 00:06:05.750
ON, because Richie was a fan of horror movies,
and one Saturday not long too after the day

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:09.490
they took down the dam, “I Was A Teenage
Werewolf was playing at the Aladdin Theater

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:10.490
in town.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:14.749
He bargains with his Dad to earn $2.50 for
mowing the lawn, though Richie claims that

00:06:14.749 --> 00:06:17.789
this is blackmail because his father knows
he wants to go to the show.

00:06:17.789 --> 00:06:23.180
Keep in mind, this was 1958, it didn’t cost
$17.50 to get into a movie, or $15 / month

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:26.999
for MoviePass to **** you in the ***. Ben
Hanscom also has no money, having spent it

00:06:26.999 --> 00:06:28.779
on junk food, so Richie spots him.

00:06:28.779 --> 00:06:30.539
Then they run into Beverly Marsh.

00:06:30.540 --> 00:06:33.110
Richie admired Bev’s looks, but mostly liked
her sense of humor.

00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:36.920
Bev doesn’t have any money, and Richie pays
for her ticket as well, since the tickets were only

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:39.770
25 cents, which they jokingly refer to as
a date.

00:06:39.770 --> 00:06:43.149
They sat on the balcony to avoid Henry Bowers
and his gang, but they were spotted on the

00:06:43.149 --> 00:06:46.960
way out and surrounded in the alley next to
the movie theater as they tried to sneak away.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:50.729
Ben led the escape effort by throwing a garbage
can to knock over Henry Bowers, and Richie

00:06:50.729 --> 00:06:54.819
ended up using the lid as a shield and blocking
a punch from Belch Huggins, helping them get

00:06:54.819 --> 00:06:55.939
free and escape.

00:06:55.939 --> 00:06:59.300
The next time Bill and Richie get together,
they decide to go to the house on Neibolt

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:02.800
Street to investigate Eddie’s story about
the encounter with It.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.400
Richie rides on the back of Bill’s bike.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:07.840
They crawl in through a broken window and discover
a coat pit in the basement.

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:12.039
The cellar door flies open and a werewolf
wearing loafers, faded jeans and a Derry High

00:07:12.039 --> 00:07:13.779
School jacket enters the room.

00:07:13.779 --> 00:07:18.300
Remember, it’s the things Richie sees in
the media that scare him, so It takes the

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.680
form of the Teenage Werewolf from the movie
he had seen.

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:24.479
I also think that because Richie is basically
the eyes of the group, whenever they are together,

00:07:24.479 --> 00:07:26.470
It usually takes the form of Richie’s fear.

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:29.270
Bill brought along his father’s gun, but
that doesn’t hurt the werewolf nearly as

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:33.289
much as Richie, who uses his Irish Cop voice
to scream at it with a sense of authority.

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:37.389
He also throws sneezing powder at the creature,
sending It into a fit -- something that would

00:07:37.389 --> 00:07:41.140
probably only work in the movies, but it works
because Richie believes in it.

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:44.990
It’s likely that It detected that Richie
is the seer of the group and tried to go for

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:45.990
his eyes.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:49.711
The two escape on Bill’s bike, and they
look back to see the clown, Pennywise, now

00:07:49.711 --> 00:07:52.289
coming after them in the Derry HS jacket.

00:07:52.289 --> 00:07:56.809
As the calendar rolled over to July, Richie
often found himself in the company of Bill,

00:07:56.809 --> 00:07:59.089
Eddie, Ben, Beverly and Stan.

00:07:59.089 --> 00:08:02.169
Henry and his gang would refer to them as
The Losers Club.

00:08:02.169 --> 00:08:06.229
On July 3rd, they got together to shoot off
fireworks when a boy named Mike Hanlon approached

00:08:06.229 --> 00:08:07.229
them.

00:08:07.229 --> 00:08:08.740
Mike was being chased by Henry Bowers.

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:13.289
The Losers Club helps defend Mike by fighting
back against the Bowers Gang by throwing rocks.

00:08:13.289 --> 00:08:17.539
Richie joins in in pelting Moose Sadler, the
tank of the opposition, and the now seven

00:08:17.539 --> 00:08:20.129
Losers are able to drive Henry and his thugs
away.

00:08:20.129 --> 00:08:23.680
That’s when they welcome Mike into the group,
and with the seven off them, the wheel is

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:24.680
complete.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:27.819
They decided to build a clubhouse in the Barrens
for protection against Bowers.

00:08:27.819 --> 00:08:31.039
Richie brought along his battery powered radio
so that they could listen to Rock and Roll

00:08:31.039 --> 00:08:32.039
while they worked.

00:08:32.039 --> 00:08:35.380
Rock and Roll is one of the few things that
both the Losers Club and the Bowers Gang seem

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:39.850
to agree on, whereas the older generation,
the parents of Derry are against it.

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:43.060
Richie is kind of the authority when it comes
to Rock music among the seven of them.

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:47.100
There seems to be a bit of a parallel between
the music and the ability to see the manifestations

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.100
of It.

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:51.650
For example, Bill’s parents are unable to
see the blood in Georgie’s room, and Beverly’s

00:08:51.650 --> 00:08:53.540
parents can’t see the blood in her bathroom.

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:56.430
In general the adults in town all turn a blind
eye to violence.

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:59.130
But the kids, the rock and rollers, can see
It.

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:02.910
The Losers Club in particular grow up and
hold on to their love of Rock and Roll, and

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:06.020
they become some of the few adults who are
still able to see It.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:10.161
One day Mike brings his father’s Derry photo
album, and Pennywise animates in one of the

00:09:10.161 --> 00:09:11.880
pictures and threatens to kill the Losers.

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:16.060
The first form It changes into is Richie’s
werewolf, because It always seems to start

00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:18.700
with the form that scares Richie, the eyes
of the group.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:22.110
Later that month, Ben Hanscom has an idea
about how they should proceed in fighting

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:23.110
back against It.

00:09:23.110 --> 00:09:25.850
He tells what he knows of the Indian smoke
ceremony.

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:28.971
Basically, Indian tribes would come together
when they had to make a big decision, and

00:09:28.971 --> 00:09:32.590
they’d sit around the fire in a smoke hole
until one of them had a vision telling them

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:33.590
what to do.

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:37.620
The Losers decide to try it inside their new
clubhouse, but the smoke is too much for Stan,

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:38.690
Ben and Eddie.

00:09:38.690 --> 00:09:41.630
Richie sees their 5 x 5 foot clubhouse expand.

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:45.810
Beverly and eventually Bill end up bailing
out as well, leaving just Richie and Mike.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:49.890
The room seemed to have expanded to the size
of a ballroom, and it was getting so smoky

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:51.910
that they could barely see each other.

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:54.360
Then, Richie felt himself float up.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:57.700
They weren’t inside anymore, they were standing
in the middle of the Barrens.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:02.720
Richie, the Seer, and Mike, the historian,
were seeing the arrival of It thousands or

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:06.580
even millions of years ago, like a movie,
only they were a part of it.

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:09.910
A burning object falls through the clouds
and Richie’s first thought was that it’s

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:10.910
a spaceship.

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:14.430
He’s able to determine this before ever
knowing that It is a cosmic creature.

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:18.060
Animals flee the area of the impact, and Richie
and Mike are pulled out of the smoke hole

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:19.060
by the others.

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:22.870
It took Richie a while to come to, and the
others admitted they didn’t think he was

00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:23.870
going to survive.

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:26.840
He threw up twice, but he had to survive to
tell the story.

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:30.400
I mean, I guess Mike could have also told
them, but it sounds a lot more believable

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.270
if the same story is coming from two people.

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:35.680
For the first time in his life, it was Richie
who could see things, and the others that

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:36.400
could not.

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:38.380
"Can only virgins see this stuff?

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:40.060
Is that why I'm not seeing this ****?"

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:44.300
...and this moment would be ingrained in his
mind for years and years come -- almost three

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:46.880
decades in fact until he needed it most.

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:54.080
Here’s a riddle for you.

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:57.470
What’s the best way to come out of an ad
break?

00:10:57.470 --> 00:10:58.920
…. With an arm break!

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.480
Eddie gets his broken by Henry --

00:11:00.480 --> 00:11:01.480
I apologize.

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:02.480
That was…

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:03.480
I’ll try not to do that again.

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:07.590
Richie is there when the Losers sneak back
to the hospital to sign Eddie’s cast while

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:08.690
his mother isn’t there.

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:12.840
Eddie’s mother is definitely not a fan of
Richie’s foul mouth and habit of smoking

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:13.840
cigarettes.

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:17.380
While they were waiting for Mrs. Kaspbrak
to **** off, they did a little target practice

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:21.950
with the slingshot at the Barrens to try to
determine who should be the one to shoot Pennywise.

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:26.110
Richie only knicked one out of ten cans, but
he held onto one of the cans the Beverly had

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:28.410
punctured as proof of concept.

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:31.700
Over the course of the rest of that July,
Richie was there to support his friends every

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:35.930
step of the way: first when Bill broke down
in the rain and screams out about how he’s

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:39.750
going to kill Pennywise, then it is Richie
and Bill who get the idea to make silver bullets

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:44.990
to fire at It, and finally on July 25th they
arrived at the 29 Neibolt house to try take

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:45.990
the clown down.

00:11:45.990 --> 00:11:49.600
In the movie, Richie freaks out when he finds
a missing poster of himself, but in the book

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:53.020
he’s just grossed out when he opens a cupboard
to find a litter of rats.

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:57.120
They get to the last door, which seems to
have been a bathroom, with white shards lying

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:01.870
everywhere from the destroyed toilet, as if
Badlands Chugs had just taken a massive **** there.

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:05.580
As always when Richie is around, the form
that it takes first is the Teenage Werewolf

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:07.380
with the high school letterman jacket.

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:11.060
Richie is the first to realize what form it’s
taking and screams out to warn the others,

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:15.030
and although the Losers take a couple of tough
shots, they are able to drive It back down

00:12:15.030 --> 00:12:16.030
into the sewers.

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:20.350
The two weeks that follow are pretty uneventful,
and consist of a lot of games of Pacheesi.

00:12:20.350 --> 00:12:24.120
The day of big confrontation with It starts
with Richie and Eddie getting popsicles in

00:12:24.120 --> 00:12:28.670
town when Bev and Ben came to warn everyone
that Henry Bowers had lost it and was trying

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:30.540
to kill her under the orders of It.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:34.310
Bill decides that now is the time to retaliate
and they climb into the sewers at the pumping

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:35.770
station in the Barrens.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:39.870
Richie is the last one to go in sees Henry
run up and slip on the puddle, so he yells,

00:12:39.870 --> 00:12:42.170
“Hey banana heels!” before climbing down.

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:45.930
When Henry tries to go in after them, Richie
bit him in the ankle before running up with

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:50.720
his friends in the drain pipe, thus fully
earning his nickname of Trashmouth Tozier.

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:53.600
"Oh OK, trash the trashmouth, I get it."

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:57.280
Eddie navigated as they searched for It’s
lair in the sewer, sometimes having to scoot

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:58.790
or crawl to fit through the pipes.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:02.470
At some point, it gradually started to get
lighter, and Richie noticed what would be

00:13:02.470 --> 00:13:07.760
the first form of It the losers would face
down in the sewers, A Giant Eye with six tentacles,

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:11.210
resembling The Crawling Eye, a horror movie
that Richie was afraid of.

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:15.190
This form combined his sensitivity to his
eyes, ommetaphobia, that I mentioned earlier,

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:19.140
and the tendency for It to use the forms of
horror movies Richie had seen to scare the

00:13:19.140 --> 00:13:20.140
entire group.

00:13:20.140 --> 00:13:23.550
They are only able to escape when Eddie, the
only one who wasn’t restrained, attacks

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:27.410
the eye by believing his aspirator was filled
with battery acid and spraying It.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:31.190
After moving on from the Crawling Eye, and
entering the lair Richie saw the rotted bodies

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:34.580
of some of the kids who had been abducted
by It during that summer, and one that really

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:38.280
hit home was Edward Corcoran, a boy who was
the same age as Richie.

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:42.000
The “true form” of It is the deadlights,
but the Losers Club’s human minds aren’t

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:45.340
able to process something like that, so they
see It as giant spider.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:49.279
Bill is successful in his mind-battle against
It in the macroverse, a fight where Richie

00:13:49.279 --> 00:13:51.520
plays a major turning point in the movie…

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:55.330
In the book version, it’s mostly just Bill
vs. It in the other dimension, but as Richie

00:13:55.330 --> 00:13:58.670
started to sense that they were coming back
from the Macroverse, a ripple went through

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:02.410
his body, sending his glasses crashing to
the floor and shattering.

00:14:02.410 --> 00:14:06.060
The Losers escape from the sewers and each
one of them partakes in The Promise, a blood

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:10.640
oath that if It should ever come back, they
would come back to try to kill It again.

00:14:10.640 --> 00:14:14.520
During this promise, Bill notices that Richie’s
face looks different without his glasses.

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:19.170
This is symbolic of the fact that after defeating
It, each Loser stops being a Loser and starts

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:22.000
transitioning into the successful adults they
would become.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:26.410
With It thrown back into a deep sleep, Richie
would no longer need to be the groups seer,

00:14:26.410 --> 00:14:30.000
and after overcoming such a huge obstacle
by defeating It, Richie would no longer be

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:34.130
bothered by trivial things, such as being
bullied for his glasses or his ommetaphobia.

00:14:34.130 --> 00:14:38.350
Also, most of the bullies were dead at this
point, so that probably helps.

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:41.420
Richie stayed close to his 6 friends, but
that would be the last time the whole group

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:43.690
got together in the same place at the same
time.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:48.960
In the Stephen King novel 11/22/63, Richie
makes a small and questionably canon appearance.

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:53.300
An English teacher named Jake Epping travels
back in time to try to prevent the assassination

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:58.279
of an American president and he ends up stopping
in Derry in the fall of 1958, approximately

00:14:58.279 --> 00:15:00.279
2 months after the Losers Club defeats It.

00:15:00.279 --> 00:15:04.080
Whenever you’re dealing with time travel,
you run the risk of creating multiple timelines.

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:06.770
Believe me, I’m a Legend of Zelda fan, I
know.

00:15:06.770 --> 00:15:10.370
So there may now be a timeline where Jake
Epping interferes, and one where he doesn’t,

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:14.590
however the Derry that Jake visits seems to
be at least very similar to the one in the

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:18.440
novel It, for example there is a mention of
Patrick Hockstetter’s body being discovered

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:20.900
in the Barrens, which lines up with the events
of It.

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:24.700
Jake discovers Beverly and Richie dancing
near the fence on the border of the Barrens

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:28.230
and is taken back by their joyfulness, perhaps
they are more relaxed than the rest of the

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:33.120
town now because they two of the seven that
realize the threat has now passed and no more

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:34.730
murders are going to take place.

00:15:34.730 --> 00:15:38.440
Bev and Richie are able to connect with Jake,
because as an outsider he seems to realize

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:41.400
the disconnected nature of most of the adults
in town.

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:44.720
Going back to my rock and roll analogy from
earlier, it would be reasonable to say Jake

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:48.380
is on the same page as them because he’s
probably grown up on rock and roll himself,

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.089
having been born in the late 70s.

00:15:50.089 --> 00:15:54.260
Also during this meeting, Beverly expresses
her belief that It is merely sleeping, so

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:58.720
it’s possible that the Losers quickly came
to this conclusion after the events of 1958.

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:02.450
They were not wrong -- Richie and the Losers
Club would eventually have to come back and

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:07.570
fulfill their promise when It rose again in
the 80s, but before that happened, Richie

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:09.180
had some growing up to do.

00:16:13.620 --> 00:16:17.460
In the 
spring of 1960, Richie’s family relocated

00:16:17.460 --> 00:16:20.810
to the Midwest, and the memories started to
fade throughout his teenage years.

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:26.490
In the year 1965, around the age of 18, Richie
switches from eyeglasses to contact lenses,

00:16:26.490 --> 00:16:30.520
thus officially completing the transition
into adulthood that began with the fall of

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:31.520
It.

00:16:31.520 --> 00:16:34.060
But his glasses would stay with him in a way
throughout his adulthood.

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:39.000
Shortly after, he started college and became
a DJ at his school radio station and was pretty

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:42.330
good at it; Richie already saw his own potential
to be great.

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:46.370
He was a hit on his campus and eventually
he moved to Hollywood to pursue his dream

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:47.370
further.

00:16:47.370 --> 00:16:50.490
The same year he moved to California he fell
in love with a woman named Sandy.

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:51.490
"She hot?"

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:54.940
Neither of them wanted Sandy to get pregnant,
so Richie got a vasectomy.

00:16:54.940 --> 00:16:58.830
Richie continued to date Sandy for another
two and a half years until a job offer sent

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:03.110
her to Washington and Richie was brought on
as a DJ for a Los Angeles FM radio station

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:04.790
called KLAD.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:08.629
One year after their breakup, Richie woke
up with the urge to get his vasectomy reversed,

00:17:08.629 --> 00:17:11.870
and went into the doctor to find out if he
could, only to discover that he had undergone

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:14.509
an extremely rare spontaneous regeneration.

00:17:14.509 --> 00:17:18.309
In other words, Richie’s sperm had been
healthy for some time, including the time

00:17:18.309 --> 00:17:19.369
he was with Sandy.

00:17:19.369 --> 00:17:23.490
Each member of the Loser’s club has unexplained
infertility, although Richie may actually

00:17:23.490 --> 00:17:27.679
be the exception to this because he’s a
smoker, he didn’t quit until 1981.

00:17:27.679 --> 00:17:31.639
Four years after that, in 1985, Richie is
at work when he receives the call from Mike

00:17:31.639 --> 00:17:34.710
Hanlon, letting him know that It had come
back.

00:17:34.710 --> 00:17:38.299
He calls his travel agent to arrange a flight,
and she asks him to do his Kinky Briefcase

00:17:38.299 --> 00:17:42.809
Sexual Accountant voice as she makes arrangements
for him at the Derry Town House hotel.

00:17:42.809 --> 00:17:47.539
His manager, Steve, chews him out for skipping
out when he's scheduled for a broadcast tomorrow

00:17:47.539 --> 00:17:49.649
where he's supposed to interview Clarence
Clemons.

00:17:49.649 --> 00:17:53.590
Without realizing it, Richie packs a bunch
of kids clothes in his suitcase, a sign of

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:56.730
the rock and roll loving comedian kid still
being alive inside of him.

00:17:56.730 --> 00:18:00.480
"Yeah, and I think the Rabbi's gonna pull
down your pants turn to the crowd and say

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:01.400
'where's the beef?'"

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:04.780
After Mike’s call, Richie’s childhood
memories start to trickle back, and in the

00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:08.570
plane ride on the way to Derry, Richie feels
the same burning sensation in his eyes that

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:11.780
he felt during the smoke hole ceremony when
he was 11 years old.

00:18:11.780 --> 00:18:15.809
As the group reconvenes, they begin to re-assume
their old roles, and Richie feels the eyes

00:18:15.809 --> 00:18:20.090
that discovered It’s origin and basically
dictated the forms of It, returning to their

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:21.480
old roles as well.

00:18:21.480 --> 00:18:24.869
After his plane lands, he drives the rest
of the way in a rental car, but he pulls over

00:18:24.869 --> 00:18:27.710
when he sees the sign for “Penobscot County,
Derry, Maine.”

00:18:27.710 --> 00:18:30.679
I’m guessing that’s NOT the same sign
that I pointed out in my Things You Missed

00:18:30.679 --> 00:18:34.620
episode on the 2019 Pet Sematary, because
that one didn’t mention Penobscot County,

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:38.659
but don’t worry all you Pet Sematary fans
out there, because when Richie pulls over,

00:18:38.659 --> 00:18:42.490
an Orinco chemical fertilizer truck roars
past him on the highway -- this is the same

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:45.850
type of truck that runs back and forth on
the road where the Creed family lives in Pet

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:46.850
Sematary.

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:50.500
But this isn’t an episode of Things You
Missed, this is Horror History, so let’s

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:52.370
continue on with the history of Richie Tozier.

00:18:52.370 --> 00:18:56.960
Richie joins Mike, Bill, Eddie, Ben and Beverly
for a reunion lunch at Jade of the Orient,

00:18:56.960 --> 00:19:01.370
where Mike fills them in on everything that’s
gone down in Derry since It’s reawakening.

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:04.990
After the meal, they receive their fortune
cookies, and each one contains a horrific

00:19:04.990 --> 00:19:08.049
surprise from Pennywise pertaining to the
person who opened it.

00:19:08.049 --> 00:19:09.139
Richie’s contains an eye.

00:19:09.139 --> 00:19:10.139
See?

00:19:10.139 --> 00:19:12.710
All that stuff I’ve been saying this entire
video wasn’t bull****.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:15.700
Everyone decides to go to a place they remember
best from Derry.

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:19.610
Richie gets into a cab, and the driver is
the same man who had taken Bill around earlier,

00:19:19.610 --> 00:19:23.710
a particularly foul-mouthed guy who constantly
adds the disclaimer, “pardon my french if

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:24.710
you’re a religious man”.

00:19:24.710 --> 00:19:26.970
I wish I got to see how this scene actually
played out.

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:29.690
Trashmouth vs trashmouth, it would have been
real interesting.

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:33.090
Richie goes back to City Center, the place
where he was nearly killed by the Paul Bunyan

00:19:33.090 --> 00:19:34.470
statue as a child.

00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:37.929
He remembered the incident that had happened
back then, then as he sees a poster, in a

00:19:37.929 --> 00:19:41.149
similar style to one of the posters for a
rock shows his mother never would have let

00:19:41.149 --> 00:19:45.049
him go to, but the concert being advertised
is for something called “Richie Tozier’s

00:19:45.049 --> 00:19:46.350
All Dead Rock Show”.

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:50.039
I think when Richie discovers his own missing
poster in the movie, this is what the director

00:19:50.039 --> 00:19:51.360
was trying to replicate.

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:54.250
When he looked back to the Paul Bunyan statue,
Paul was no longer there.

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:58.690
In his place, was a giant plastic version
of Pennywise, the dancing Clown, and the lips

00:19:58.690 --> 00:20:03.049
bleeding with red paint parted to reveal huge,
razor pointed teeth.

00:20:03.049 --> 00:20:06.639
This time, however, when Richie ran for it,
he could hear Pennywise’s voice booming

00:20:06.639 --> 00:20:07.639
after him.

00:20:07.639 --> 00:20:11.169
He made it to the sidewalk to see that the
statue had been replaced yet again, this time

00:20:11.169 --> 00:20:13.639
with one of his favorite rock idols, Buddy
Holly.

00:20:13.639 --> 00:20:17.499
He feels an immense pain in one of his contacts
and blinks it out of his eye.

00:20:17.499 --> 00:20:21.340
All returns to normal, but Richie can still
hear the laughter of Pennywise echoing in

00:20:21.340 --> 00:20:22.340
his head.

00:20:22.340 --> 00:20:26.200
That night they all reconvened in the library
for drinks and remenissions when Richie has

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:29.790
an epiphany, and he remembers seeing the arrival
of It in the smoke hole for the first time

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:30.929
since he was a kid.

00:20:30.929 --> 00:20:34.659
When this happens, he reaches to push his
glasses up on his nose, temporarily forgetting

00:20:34.659 --> 00:20:38.260
that he’s been wearing contacts for the
last 20 years and once again, he feels the

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:39.419
smoke in his eyes.

00:20:39.419 --> 00:20:42.919
Before they leave, scars on their hands that
were cut for the blood oath all those years

00:20:42.919 --> 00:20:47.960
ago reopen, and everyone joins hands, causing
the inside of the library to go into a whirlwind

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:48.960
of their power.

00:20:48.960 --> 00:20:52.190
Richie goes back to the hotel, and starts
to fall asleep when he receives a phone call

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:54.730
from Beverly asking him to come to Eddie’s
room.

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:58.600
Without asking questions, he shows up to a
room with a maimed Eddie Kaspbrak and a dead

00:20:58.600 --> 00:20:59.640
Henry Bowers.

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:03.259
They find out that Mike was attacked before
he left the library, so Richie calls the hospital

00:21:03.259 --> 00:21:06.590
using his news reporter voice to gather the
information that the police chief wouldn’t

00:21:06.590 --> 00:21:07.590
give out to them.

00:21:07.590 --> 00:21:09.360
The group decides that enough was enough.

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:13.940
It was responsible for the suicide of their
friend Stan, and possibly the death of Mike.

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:15.539
Eddie had also been injured.

00:21:15.539 --> 00:21:19.440
The only thing left for them to do was to
kill that ****ing clown.

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:23.230
Richie took the wheel and Beverly, Eddie,
Bill and Ben piled into the limousine that

00:21:23.230 --> 00:21:24.320
Eddie had driven to Derry.

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:27.809
Their destination was the Barrens, the place
where they had climbed down into the sewers

00:21:27.809 --> 00:21:30.309
to try to kill It 27 years ago.

00:21:30.309 --> 00:21:34.549
Pennywise uses the car radio to taunt and
threaten them, first doing an ad read for

00:21:34.549 --> 00:21:36.230
the Richie Tozier All-Dead Rock show.

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:39.580
That reminds me, it’s time for me to play
an ad as well, but don’t go away, because

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:43.100
Richie Tozier plays a hand in the final showdown
with It.

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:44.320
Literally.

00:21:52.260 --> 00:21:55.820
Richie parks the limo next to the bridge,
and they go to the pumping station where they

00:21:55.820 --> 00:21:57.630
had entered the sewers once before.

00:21:57.630 --> 00:22:01.889
The machinery had been turned off, and they
were able to descend into the sewers, trudge

00:22:01.889 --> 00:22:05.989
and crawl their way through dirty water and
sewage, eventually finding the inner lair

00:22:05.989 --> 00:22:06.989
of It.

00:22:06.989 --> 00:22:09.889
Again, their minds are unable to process the
deadlights, but this time they’re able to

00:22:09.889 --> 00:22:13.919
tell that there is some other shape behind
the spider, which is described as being “like

00:22:13.919 --> 00:22:17.080
someone moving behind a movie screen,” which
I find interesting because of the tendency

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:20.100
of It to take the form of the monsters Richie
has seen in movies.

00:22:20.100 --> 00:22:24.879
The spider comes for Bill and the ritual begins
once again, Bill and It engage in an out of

00:22:24.879 --> 00:22:26.919
body showdown in the macroverse.

00:22:26.919 --> 00:22:30.520
This time, it doesn’t go as well for Bill,
the celestial being known as The Turtle is

00:22:30.520 --> 00:22:31.880
no longer there to help him.

00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:35.970
Richie notices this back in the chamber, because
he sees Bill’s face contort as if his spirit

00:22:35.970 --> 00:22:37.570
is in pain or struggling.

00:22:37.570 --> 00:22:41.929
All along Richie has been the support for
Bill: the photo album, 29 Neibolt and the

00:22:41.929 --> 00:22:44.720
stormy afternoon in the Barrens being a few
examples.

00:22:44.720 --> 00:22:48.600
Richie runs up to the spider’s stinger and
uses his Irish Cop voice to distract it.

00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:53.140
He gets whacked into the darkness by It and
joins Bill in the Macroverse, where he does

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:55.200
what Bill was unable to this time around.

00:22:55.200 --> 00:22:58.159
He bites into It’s metaphysical tongue and
hangs on tight.

00:22:58.159 --> 00:23:01.429
He flies past the shell of The Turtle, possibly
its corpse.

00:23:01.429 --> 00:23:04.690
He approaches another barrier, but he can't
grasp the shape, but he thinks it could be

00:23:04.690 --> 00:23:06.460
a wall of steaks.

00:23:06.460 --> 00:23:08.130
No, not those stakes.

00:23:08.130 --> 00:23:09.269
These stakes.

00:23:09.269 --> 00:23:12.529
Maybe a reference to It appearing to Ben in
the form of Dracula one time?

00:23:12.529 --> 00:23:16.489
Richie finds Bill and takes his hand, then
turns the tables on It and threatens to kill

00:23:16.489 --> 00:23:19.980
It right then and there if It doesn’t bring
them back to the physical world.

00:23:19.980 --> 00:23:24.629
Richie uses his mind to hang on tight to It,
nearly losing his grip before arriving back

00:23:24.629 --> 00:23:26.320
in the actual spider’s chamber.

00:23:26.320 --> 00:23:30.169
When they come back they find Eddie seriously
injured, as he had tried to attack It with

00:23:30.169 --> 00:23:35.309
his aspirator as he did to the Crawling Eye
in 1958, but he got his arm dismembered and

00:23:35.309 --> 00:23:37.419
was bleeding out on the floor of the chamber.

00:23:37.419 --> 00:23:39.600
[“—eds—”
“—eds oh my god Bill, Ben, someone he’s

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:43.700
lost his arm, his—” He looked up at Beverly
and saw she was crying, the tears coursing

00:23:43.700 --> 00:23:45.419
down her dirty cheeks.

00:23:45.419 --> 00:23:46.419
“Richie...”

00:23:46.419 --> 00:23:47.419
“What?”

00:23:47.419 --> 00:23:48.830
Richie was down on his hands and knees, staring
at him desperately.

00:23:48.830 --> 00:23:51.429
“Don’t call me Eds,” he said, and smiled.]

00:23:51.429 --> 00:23:53.669
Those would be Eddie’s final words.

00:23:53.669 --> 00:23:57.120
Beverly took him in her arms and urged Richie,
who wanted to stay and comfort Eddie in his

00:23:57.120 --> 00:24:01.429
final moments, to go on after the spider so
that It doesn’t come back after another

00:24:01.429 --> 00:24:02.429
27 years.

00:24:02.429 --> 00:24:05.049
"If that thing comes back when I'm 70..."

00:24:05.049 --> 00:24:06.139
"Let's finish it."

00:24:06.139 --> 00:24:07.600
"Once and for all."

00:24:07.600 --> 00:24:10.720
Bill and Richie chased It into the deepest
part of the chamber, further than they had

00:24:10.720 --> 00:24:11.720
ever been before.

00:24:11.720 --> 00:24:16.710
It begs them to let It go, offering them power,
success and long lives beyond their wildest

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:17.710
dreams.

00:24:17.710 --> 00:24:19.510
They both simultaneously plunged into It.

00:24:19.510 --> 00:24:23.659
The monster lashed out at them, injuring Richie
who struggled not to drown in It’s guts.

00:24:23.659 --> 00:24:27.230
Bill ended it when he crushed the heart of
It in his hands, where it exploded.

00:24:27.230 --> 00:24:30.659
Bill took Richie in his arms and tried to
find Beverly and Ben in the dark, since the

00:24:30.659 --> 00:24:33.880
deadlights that had been illuminating the
place died along with the spider.

00:24:33.880 --> 00:24:35.700
When they reconvene, Richie comes back to.

00:24:35.700 --> 00:24:39.859
The tunnel they are in starts shaking, a side
effect of the violent storm taking place above

00:24:39.859 --> 00:24:40.859
them.

00:24:40.859 --> 00:24:43.999
They have to leave Eddie behind in order to
try to save Bill’s wife Audra, and Richie

00:24:43.999 --> 00:24:48.259
carries her for a bit as they make their way
back to the surface, perhaps his final gesture

00:24:48.259 --> 00:24:50.510
of support towards his friend Bill.

00:24:50.510 --> 00:24:54.419
Richie flew back to California a few days
later, and after the defeat of It, each member

00:24:54.419 --> 00:24:57.940
of the Losers Club gradually started to lose
their memories of everything that had happened

00:24:57.940 --> 00:24:58.940
in Derry.

00:24:58.940 --> 00:25:01.749
Later in the week, Mike Hanlon gave Richie
a call in Beverly Hills.

00:25:01.749 --> 00:25:05.630
At first it went to the answering machine,
and when Richie picked it up, he said let

00:25:05.630 --> 00:25:09.320
Mike talk to the answering machine as long
as he did because for a slight moment, he

00:25:09.320 --> 00:25:13.200
had no idea who Mike was -- just like when
Mike first reached out to tell his old friends

00:25:13.200 --> 00:25:14.610
that It had come back.

00:25:14.610 --> 00:25:18.970
Richie Tozier was a joker and a troublemaker,
but he played an important part in the group,

00:25:18.970 --> 00:25:23.090
using his eyes and his creative voice impressions
to help them stand a chance against It, and

00:25:23.090 --> 00:25:25.359
he was always there for his pals when they
needed him.

00:25:25.359 --> 00:25:29.419
Kind of like how I’m going to be here, for
you, the viewers, with more episodes of Horror

00:25:29.419 --> 00:25:33.359
History, just click the playlist on the left
to see me analyse more characters like Bill

00:25:33.359 --> 00:25:35.320
Denbrough, Stan Uris and others.

00:25:35.320 --> 00:25:39.840
And remember to subscribe to CZsWorld for
new horrors every week and ring the deathbell

00:25:39.840 --> 00:25:42.799
for notifications, so even if you do lose
your memories, I’ll still be able to see

00:25:42.799 --> 00:25:44.309
you in the next one.

00:25:44.309 --> 00:25:46.309
Assuming we both survive.

